{{also|low-down}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|low-down}}
* {{l|en|low down}}

===Etymology===
Compound adjective of {{compound|en|low|down}} in the sense of "[[humble]]" recorded in the 1540s, in the sense of "[[vulgar]], far down the social scale" in 1888. Recorded as a noun in 1915 in the slang sense of secret or [[inside information]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[inside information]], the [[story]] or [[truth]].
#: {{syn|en|scoop|dirt|dope|straight dope|poop}}
#: {{ux|en|All the reporters hoped to be the first to get the '''lowdown''' on the celebrity's marriage plans.}}
#: {{ux|en|here's the '''lowdown'''}}
#: {{ux|en|to give somebody the '''lowdown'''}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1985|title=Can’t Get There From Here|album=Fables of the Reconstruction|artist=R.E.M.|text=Lawyer Jeff, he knows the '''low-down''' / It’s mighty bad to visit home}}
# A [[lowlife]], a despicable person.

